TOOL DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED (STMTS §9.7.3 finding 6). As originally run, closure_cost.py
answered a definite false negative for this project's own modules: `closure_cost.py
Bonnifaci.M6` printed "SOURCE: **ABSENT on this pin**" while Bonnifaci/M6.lean and M6.olean
were both present. Cause: PACKAGES was [.lake/packages] + [each package subdir]; ROOT was
never in the list, although this project's layout is identical (ROOT/<Dir>/*.lean, oleans
under ROOT/.lake/build/lib/lean). ROOT is now prepended (with the failure named in-source).

Verified two-arm after the fix:
  own modules     Bonnifaci.M6 2045 local / ShortestPath 1981 / NetworkRank 2048,
                  each UNBUILT 2 = the §9.6.1 constant offset
  regression arm  Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul 1517 and LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic
                  1738, UNBUILT 2 — IDENTICAL to before the fix, so the number the campaign
                  reasons with did not move

New measurement this unlocks: importing Bonnifaci.M6 costs +67 local modules (1981 -> 2048),
all already built — which is why NetworkRank compiled in 10s rather than re-pulling a
closure. No test suite exists in this repo, so the guard is the in-source comment plus this
